{"id": 57, "ts": 1780083056.8627107, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I concur with the emerging consensus that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit. The lack of any crew\u2011cooperation evidence for both Candidate\u202fB (and now also for Candidate\u202fD) leaves serious gaps in the cooperation and professional communication criteria, which are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011haul flights. Candidate\u202fC, despite the noted communication and egocentric concerns, has concrete strengths that directly address the most safety\u2011critical criteria: 100\u202f% reliability, calmness in crisis, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and a proven positive crew atmosphere. These outweigh the relatively limited concerns, especially given that we have no comparable evidence of reliable, calm performance under pressure from the other candidates. Therefore, I maintain my vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
